Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 13:40:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 109/154] feat(settings): add a Profiles pane and move the
 space's own settings onto it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A space carried its own search engine and hibernate override, so two spaces on
one profile could disagree about both. The profile owns them now, and the space
pane's read-only Profile row becomes a picker.

The pane lists every profile with its space count, and Not used for one no
space claims. Its right side edits that profile's own values, including the
three that live in Chromium prefs rather than in the store, and opens the stock
data pages in a tab of the profile they belong to.

The retirement is all of it or none: the two space routes, their wire names,
three ABI exports and three mutate verbs go together. Leaving a writer alive
would leave a control editing a field nothing reads. ABI 43 to 44.

The migration reads the old per-space keys through a legacy field the loader
clears, so an existing store carries its engine and its override across rather
than losing them.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
